# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Credentials. The server stores its session and refresh tokens under the user's
# config directory, never in the repo, but keep a hard guard here anyway.
.env
.env.*
credentials.json
*.token
.homey-mcp/

# Anything captured from a real Homey stays on the machine that captured it.
#
# raw/   verbatim captures: device names, LAN addresses, cloud ids, the names of
#        the people living there.
# local/ pseudonymised captures. Safer, but still publishes the shape of a real
#        household: how many rooms, which apps, which kinds of device. That is
#        nobody else's business either, so it does not get committed.
#
# The fixtures that DO ship are hand-built from measured behaviour and contain no
# household data at all. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
tests/fixtures/raw/
tests/fixtures/local/
scratch/
*.local.json

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
